CORE
unpacked_array_element_width1.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.c\.p_in\] always main\.c\.i\[0\] == 22'h3FF: PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p0\] always \(##1 main\.x\[0\] == 21'h1FFFFF\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^\[main\.p1\] always main\.z\[0\] == 22'h3FF: PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Unpacked arrays with element types of different widths are assignment
compatible; the elements are truncated or extended, in assignments and in
input and output port connections.
